VTID-03952 — commands.log
==========================

## Environment constraint (recorded up front, honestly)

$ cd services/gateway && npm ci
-> fails: 403 Forbidden against https://registry.npmjs.org (org egress
   policy in this sandboxed session denies the npm registry). No
   node_modules could be installed, so neither `tsc --noEmit` nor the
   gateway's vitest/jest suite could be run locally in this session.
   This is why AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 above are marked as manual-diff-review
   verified rather than automated-test verified, and why this workflow's
   own Build Gate step (which runs in CI, not this sandbox) is the first
   real `npm ci && npm run build` on this diff.

## Investigation (read-only, no writes)

- Delegated two read-only background research agents (frontend + gateway)
  to trace the full click-to-loaded-screen login sequence, independently.
  Frontend agent found: MaxinaPortal.tsx's handleSignIn() called
  switch_to_tenant_by_slug + refreshSession(), then a SECOND effect
  (setTenantBySlug('maxina')) repeated the same RPC+refresh moments later;
  4 distinct full-screen loading gates in sequence
  (AuthGuard -> Index/useSmartRouting -> OnboardingWelcome -> AppLayout);
  the `profiles` table fetched independently 3+ times with no shared
  cache. Gateway agent found: `/auth/login` awaits 4 sequential DB reads
  where none depend on each other's result; `/auth/me` awaits 6-7
  sequential reads including one whose own comment claims "Parallel
  fetch" while the code is a plain sequential `await`.
- Read `services/gateway/src/routes/auth.ts` directly to confirm both
  findings against the real source (not just the agents' summaries)
  before editing anything.

## Implementation

- Edited services/gateway/src/routes/auth.ts:
  - POST /login: wrapped the app_users + users profile reads in
    `Promise.all`.
  - POST /login: wrapped the tenant-membership/welcome-notification
    decision block in a fire-and-forget `void (async () => {...})()
    .catch(...)` IIFE, moving it off the awaited response path.
  - GET /me: wrapped the 4 independent reads (app_users profile,
    profiles.vitana_id_locked/registration_seq, users fallback,
    user_tenants memberships) in `Promise.all`.

## Merge-conflict handling (recorded because it changed the diff's shape)

- Pushed the branch and opened the PR against an origin/main that (per a
  shallow git clone in this session hiding the real merge-base) appeared
  to have already diverged. `git merge origin/main` first failed with
  "refusing to merge unrelated histories" — resolved with
  `git fetch --unshallow origin`, after which a real merge-base was found
  and a normal 3-way merge succeeded.
- The real origin/main had, in the interim, merged an unrelated PR
  (VTID-03827, Aurora/Cognito auth cutover) that reintroduced the
  `services/gateway/src/routes/auth-repository.ts` (`repo.*`) data-access
  seam this branch's edits were written against in the first place. After
  the merge, re-applied the exact same three edits (Promise.all wrapping)
  onto the post-merge file structure — no logic beyond the original
  parallelization intent was changed.
- Self-caught and fixed a real mistake here: the first attempt staged the
  clean post-merge file via `git add` BEFORE re-applying the edits via the
  Edit tool, then committed the STAGED (pre-edit) content — so the first
  pushed merge commit silently dropped the fix. Caught this by diffing
  `git show HEAD:services/gateway/src/routes/auth.ts` against the known
  fix markers before considering the merge done; a session stop-hook
  git-status check also flagged the resulting uncommitted working-tree
  diff. Fixed with a follow-up commit containing the actual re-applied
  change, verified present in the pushed tree before reporting done.

